menu "Artemis HID configuration"

    config ARTEMIS_HID_INCLUDE_TOUCH
        bool "Include the absolute touchscreen (digitizer) interface"
        default y
        help
            Android can use an external absolute touchscreen. iOS does not
            support external HID digitizers, so an iOS-only build should
            disable this and expose keyboard + mouse only.

endmenu

    config ARTEMIS_HID_BCI_ONLY
        bool "Expose only the Apple BCI HID interface (absolute pointer spike)"
        default n
        help
            Build a BCI-only HID device for iOS 26+. The device exposes one
            BCI HID interface: Report ID 2 (32 buttons) and Report ID 3
            (absolute x/y/z pointer). Touch, boot mouse and keyboard are
            omitted. This is a hardware-validation spike, not the default rig.
